needs-decision: [key=arrow-lr] no-mistakes review gate, finding review-3 (ask-user, warning, src/components/planning/location-picker.tsx). Verbatim: "Simplification: the ArrowRight and ArrowLeft branches in the picker's keyboard handler are an unrequired second spelling of gestures the control already has. The intent specifies \"Arrow keys move, Enter on a node that has children EXPANDS the next level\" and \"Escape steps back one level, then closes\" - ArrowRight duplicates Enter-on-a-parent and ArrowLeft duplicates Escape-steps-back, and neither appears in the intent or in `dropdown.tsx`'s shared `dropdownKeyDown` conventions the intent told the author to reuse. No requirement needs them; recommend removing both cases rather than keeping and ... (truncated by the tool at 783 chars)". CONTEXT: I added ArrowRight/ArrowLeft as pointer-free aliases (ArrowRight = descend, ArrowLeft = step back a level) on top of the specified Enter/Escape. They are untested and unspecified. A follow-up task will add L/O keys to the bar menu using this component. OPTIONS: (A) fix - remove both branches, keeping only the spec'd Enter/Escape/Space/typing; (B) approve - keep them as a convenience and I add tests for them. The other 4 findings are auto-fix and all real misses of mine (keyboard reopen does not reset the drill path; stale "It takes this experiment's project" copy in flow-editor.tsx; listLocationTree over-fetching data/registry_id; leftover createProject mock in entry-editor.test.tsx) - I will fix those in the same round once you decide (A) or (B).
