needs-decision: [key=picker-props] no-mistakes FIX-REVIEW gate, finding review-2 (ask-user, warning, src/components/planning/location-picker.tsx). Verbatim: "Simplification: the picker introduces two optional props no call site uses and the intent does not ask for. The intent names the prop list as `{ value, onChange, nodes, disabled?, reason? }`; `className` (line 58) and the `aria-label` OVERRIDE (line 59) are beyond it, and neither `task-composer.tsx:753` nor `schedule-panel.tsx:737` passes either. (`reason` is also unpassed but is intent-specified, so it stays.) The constant default `aria-label=\"Location\"` is load-bearing - the tests and the ui-sweep select on it - so the narrower form is a fixed `aria-label=\"Location\"` and no `className` prop ... (truncated by the tool at 760 chars)". VERIFIED: both call sites pass only value/onChange/nodes/disabled, so both props are dead today. FOR REMOVING: YAGNI, and the brief told me to export the component cleanly. AGAINST: the brief also says a follow-up task adds L/O keys to the bar menu using this component, and a third mount point is the case where a `className` would plausibly be wanted; re-adding it later is a one-line change either way. My recommendation is REMOVE (option A) - a prop with no caller cannot be shown to work, and the fixed aria-label the reviewer proposes keeps the tests and the ui-sweep probe selecting on it. OPTIONS: (A) fix - drop `className` and the `aria-label` override, hard-code aria-label="Location", keep `reason`; (B) approve - keep both as forward-looking API.
needs-decision: [key=sweep-dimensions] SAME GATE, additional defect I found while verifying review-1 and which the reviewer did NOT catch in full. review-1 (auto-fix) says scripts/ui-sweep.mjs DIMENSIONS still lists "Project", which is now a no-op so two checks per theme re-measure the previous iteration (Tag) under a false label. TRUE, and worse: the View panel actually renders Progress / Record / Tag / Operator / Location (DIMENSION_LABEL in colour-by.ts), while the sweep array is ["Status","Tag","Project","Operator","Location"]. So "Status" is ALSO a silent no-op and "Progress" - the default dimension - is never swept at all. The "Status" half is pre-existing, not introduced by me; the "Project" half is mine. This matters because it means 4 of the 82 checks I cited as browser-verification evidence in docs/verification/ prove nothing. I can fold the full correction into this same fix round via --add-finding. OPTIONS: (A) fix the whole array to ["Progress","Record","Tag","Operator","Location"] so every labelled check measures the panel it names; (B) fix only "Project" per the reviewer and leave the pre-existing "Status"/"Progress" gap for its owner. I recommend (A): the fix agent is editing that line anyway, and leaving a known-false check beside a corrected one is the worse outcome. Holding the gate until both keys come back.
resolved: [key=sweep-dimensions] captain chose Option A - DIMENSIONS corrected to [Progress, Record, Tag, Operator, Location] via --add-finding in this fix round; sweep re-run and docs/verification evidence refresh to follow
